{#
  THE DOOR — the scanner a steward holds at the entrance.

  ── WHY THIS TEMPLATE DOES NOT EXTEND layout/gates.twig ────────────────────
  It used to, and that put the ENTIRE SITE on a door: the desktop nav, the footer, the
  community FAB, the Gee launcher, and — because `.ag-nav` hides below 900px and
  `.ag-mobnav` takes over — a bottom tab bar under the steward's thumb offering Home,
  Pulse, Nominate, Ranks and Menu. On a phone, mid-queue, the largest tap targets on the
  door were five ways to leave it.

  So this is a standalone document that loads one stylesheet. It is not an optimisation;
  it is the first thing the redesign fixes.

  ── EVERY TIME HERE IS PRE-FORMATTED BY THE CONTROLLER ─────────────────────
  In the EVENT's own zone. These were once `|slice(11, 5)` over the stored string, and
  storage is UTC by this application's convention — so a gate closing at 23:00 in Lagos
  told its steward it closed at 22:00. Slicing a datetime is not formatting it; it is
  reading the storage convention out loud. Nothing below formats a time.

  ── THE THREE RULES THE OLD PAGE WAS BUILT ON, AND WHERE THEY WENT ─────────
    1. "The verdict is a WORD before it is a colour." KEPT, and strengthened: every state
       has its own word AND its own mark glyph, so the colour is confirmation. The
       redesign adds that the whole FRAME carries the hue, because a steward reads it at
       arm's length in the dark and colour arrives before typography.
    2. "The typed box is the door, not the fallback." REVERSED, deliberately. The camera
       is now the ground state and the keypad is behind `123` — because the two reasons
       the camera never worked in production were a `Permissions-Policy` header and a
       feature gate on `BarcodeDetector`, and both are fixed. The keypad is kept for the
       wet lens and for iOS, and it is one tap away.
    3. "Nothing reloads." KEPT. A page load per attendee IS the queue.
#}<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="dr-html">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
{# `viewport-fit=cover` so the dock can pad past the home indicator rather than under it. #}
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#04080a">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
<title>{{ page_title|default('Door — Africa GATES') }}</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('/assets/css/components/door.css') }}">
{% if ok %}
{# The organiser's own accent, lifted by DoorTone until it clears the dark frame. Three
   values and not one: `accent` owes 3:1 as a user-interface component (the sweep, the
   torch, the rule, the mark), `accent_text` owes 4.5:1 because a guest of honour's name
   is 21px at weight 500 and somebody has to read it, and `soft` is the sweep gradient's
   mid stop as a resolved rgba — a browser that does not know color-mix() drops the whole
   background declaration and takes the scan line with it. #}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
.dr{--dr-accent:{{ tone.accent }};--dr-accent-text:{{ tone.accent_text }};--dr-accent-soft:{{ tone.soft }}}
</style>
{% endif %}
</head>
<body class="dr-body">

{% if not ok %}
  {# ── THE PASS IS DEAD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Camera off, light out. A dead gate should look dead — there is nothing this person
     can do but read the time, so the screen gives them the time and nothing else. It is
     still a PAGE and not a 404, because somebody is standing at a door and "this opens at
     18:00" is the difference between waiting two minutes and ringing an organiser. #}
  <div class="dr" data-state="closed">
    <div class="dr__shut">
      <span class="dr__shut__m" aria-hidden="true">✕</span>
      <p class="dr__shut__k">This pass</p>
      <p class="dr__shut__w">{{ reason == 'early' ? 'Not open yet' : 'Door closed' }}</p>
      {% if reason == 'early' and opens_at %}
        <p class="dr__shut__l">It opens at {{ opens_at }}</p>
      {% elseif closes_at %}
        <p class="dr__shut__l">It closed at {{ closes_at }}</p>
      {% endif %}
      <p class="dr__shut__b">
        {{ message }}
        {%- if opens_at and closes_at %} Valid from {{ opens_at }} to {{ closes_at }}.{% endif %}
        Ask whoever sent the link for a new one.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

{% else %}

<div class="dr" id="dr" data-state="idle">

  {# The light. Two blurred fields drifting on unequal cycles behind everything, a
     hairline rim, and one flare per scan that settles by itself. Every colour in here
     comes from the custom properties `data-state` sets. #}
  <div class="dr__aura" id="drAura" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="dr__vig" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="dr__rim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {# ── THE VIEWFINDER, WHICH IS THE GROUND STATE ────────────────────────
     The camera never leaves. A verdict FREEZES and dims it rather than emptying the
     frame, so the screen reads as held rather than blank. #}
  <div class="dr__feed" id="drFeed" aria-hidden="true">
    <video class="dr__video" id="drVideo" playsinline muted autoplay></video>
    <div class="dr__reticle"><i class="dr__sweep" id="drSweep"></i></div>
  </div>

  {# The camera is started on load, but a browser may refuse to open one without a
     gesture and every browser may refuse without permission. Rather than a dead black
     rectangle, the reticle itself becomes the button — one tap, in the place the
     steward is already looking. #}
  <button type="button" class="dr__tap" id="drTap" hidden>
    <span class="dr__tap__t" id="drTapT">Tap to start the camera</span>
  </button>

  <header class="dr__head">
    <div class="dr__head__l">
      <p class="dr__ev">{{ event.title }}</p>
      <p class="dr__gate">
        {{- label ?: 'Door' }}{% if closes_short %} · closes {{ closes_short }}{% endif -%}
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="dr__tally">
      <span id="drCount">{{ admitted }}</span><i>/{{ expected }}</i>
      <span class="dr__sr" aria-live="polite" id="drCountSr">{{ admitted }} of {{ expected }} in</span>
    </p>
  </header>

  {# Scans taken while the line was down. A hairline under the header, never a chip. #}
  <div class="dr__held" id="drHeld" hidden>
    <span class="dr__held__t" id="drHeldT"></span>
    <button type="button" class="dr__held__b" id="drSend">Send</button>
  </div>

  <div class="dr__spacer"></div>

  {# ── THE VERDICT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     `aria-live="assertive"` because it interrupts for a reason: the steward is looking
     at a person, not at the phone, and this is the one thing on the screen that must
     reach them without being looked for. #}
  <section class="dr__slab" id="drSlab" role="status" aria-live="assertive" hidden>
    <i class="dr__slab__rule" id="drRule" aria-hidden="true"></i>

    <div class="dr__vh">
      <span class="dr__mark" id="drMark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="dr__kicker" id="drKicker"></span>
      <span class="dr__code" id="drCode"></span>
      <button type="button" class="dr__x" id="drDismiss" aria-label="Back to scanning">✕</button>
    </div>

    <p class="dr__word" id="drWord"></p>
    <p class="dr__name" id="drName" hidden></p>
    <p class="dr__meta" id="drMeta" hidden></p>

    {# A multi-seat ticket with more than one seat free admits NOBODY until a count is
       chosen. Guests of honour skip it entirely. #}
    <div class="dr__party" id="drParty" role="group" aria-label="How many are here" hidden></div>

    {# Two taps, no dialog. A modal at a door is a second thing to dismiss one-handed
       with a queue waiting, and the relabel carries what a confirm box would. #}
    <button type="button" class="dr__undo" id="drUndo" hidden>Not them — take it back</button>
  </section>

  <div class="dr__dock">
    <button type="button" class="dr__circ" id="drTorch" aria-label="Torch" aria-pressed="false">☀</button>
    {# Hidden unless the browser has actually refused a greeting. A control that is always
       there would be one more thing on a screen a steward glances at with a queue in front
       of them, and for most of them there is nothing to fix. #}
    <button type="button" class="dr__circ dr__circ--sound" id="drSound"
            aria-label="Let the door greet guests aloud" hidden>♪</button>
    <button type="button" class="dr__arr" id="drOpenLog">
      <span class="dr__arr__last" id="drLast">Nothing scanned yet tonight</span>
      <span class="dr__arr__w">Arrivals</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="dr__circ dr__circ--pad" id="drOpenPad" aria-label="Type a code instead">123</button>
  </div>

  {# ── THE KEYPAD — kept because iOS Safari has no BarcodeDetector and lenses get wet.
     A fallback, never the default. #}
  <div class="dr__pad" id="drPad" hidden>
    <div class="dr__pad__h">
      <p class="dr__pad__l" id="drPadL">Type it instead</p>
      <button type="button" class="dr__x" id="drClosePad" aria-label="Close the keypad">✕</button>
    </div>
    <form class="dr__pad__f" id="drForm" autocomplete="off">
      <input class="dr__pad__i" id="drInput" name="code" placeholder="ABCD-2468"
             aria-labelledby="drPadL" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false"
             autocapitalize="characters" inputmode="latin" maxlength="64">
      <button type="submit" class="dr__pad__go" id="drGo">Check</button>
    </form>
  </div>

  {# ── ARRIVALS — every admission, refusal and reversal, newest first ────
     Seeded from `gates_event_checkin_log` so a steward taking over a gate mid-evening
     sees what happened before they arrived, rather than an empty list that reads as
     "nobody has come in". #}
  <div class="dr__log" id="drLog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Arrivals" hidden>
    <div class="dr__log__h">
      <p class="dr__log__t">Arrivals</p>
      <p class="dr__log__n" id="drLogN"></p>
      <button type="button" class="dr__x dr__x--lg" id="drCloseLog" aria-label="Close arrivals">✕</button>
    </div>
    <div class="dr__log__b">
      <p class="dr__log__e" id="drLogE" hidden>Nobody yet tonight. Every admission, refusal and reversal is written here as it happens.</p>
      <div id="drRows"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
(function () {
  'use strict';

  // Captured HERE, synchronously. `document.currentScript` is only set during a script's
  // initial pass — read inside a click handler it is null, and the decoder injected below
  // would carry an empty nonce.
  var NONCE = (document.currentScript && document.currentScript.nonce) || '';

  var TOKEN = {{ token|json_encode|raw }};
  var URL_CHECK = '/door/' + TOKEN + '/check';
  var URL_UNDO  = '/door/' + TOKEN + '/undo';
  var URL_SYNC  = '/door/' + TOKEN + '/sync';

  var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };
  var root = $('dr'), aura = $('drAura'), slab = $('drSlab');
  if (!root || !slab) return;

  var el = {
    feed: $('drFeed'), video: $('drVideo'), sweep: $('drSweep'), tap: $('drTap'), tapT: $('drTapT'),
    count: $('drCount'), countSr: $('drCountSr'),
    held: $('drHeld'), heldT: $('drHeldT'), send: $('drSend'),
    rule: $('drRule'), mark: $('drMark'), kicker: $('drKicker'), code: $('drCode'),
    word: $('drWord'), name: $('drName'), meta: $('drMeta'),
    party: $('drParty'), undo: $('drUndo'), dismiss: $('drDismiss'),
    torch: $('drTorch'), openLog: $('drOpenLog'), last: $('drLast'), openPad: $('drOpenPad'),
    sound: $('drSound'),
    pad: $('drPad'), form: $('drForm'), input: $('drInput'), go: $('drGo'), closePad: $('drClosePad'),
    log: $('drLog'), logN: $('drLogN'), logE: $('drLogE'), rows: $('drRows'), closeLog: $('drCloseLog')
  };

  // ══ THE VOICE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  //
  // One <audio> element, reused. Created ONCE AND EAGERLY, and this is the whole of why
  // the greeting never played: the element used to be built lazily inside greet(), which
  // runs from the decode loop. So the only element that ever existed was created outside
  // a user gesture, was never once played inside one, and every browser that gates
  // audible playback refused it — as a rejected promise the catch below swallows, which
  // is the right thing to do with it and is exactly why nobody saw this. No error, no
  // console line, no log: a room of people never hearing their names.
  //
  // (The other half was a HEADER. `Permissions-Policy: autoplay=()` denied the feature to
  // our own pages site-wide, so the refusal came before any of this ran — the same shape
  // as the `camera=()` that had the ticket scanner dead. Fixed in
  // SecurityHeadersMiddleware::SHARED and public/.htaccess together.)
  //
  // The src is a key the server rendered HOURS ago by a maintenance sweep. Nothing is
  // synthesised here and nothing is awaited: play() is fired and forgotten, so a slow
  // clip, a muted phone or a refused autoplay cannot hold up the verdict or the queue.
  var welcomeOn = {{ welcome_on|default(false) ? 'true' : 'false' }};
  var primeKey  = {{ (welcome_prime|default(''))|json_encode|raw }};
  var audio     = welcomeOn ? new Audio() : null;
  var unlocked  = false;
  var pending   = '';                       // a greeting refused, waiting on one tap

  if (audio) audio.preload = 'none';

  function clipUrl(key) { return '/door/' + TOKEN + '/welcome/' + key; }

  /**
   * Bank the steward's first touch, whatever they touched.
   *
   * MUTED, so the torch button does not answer with "You are welcome." — the point is
   * only that this element has been played inside a gesture once. After that the decode
   * loop may play it audibly for the rest of the evening.
   */
  function unlock() {
    if (!audio || unlocked || !primeKey) return;
    unlocked = true;
    try {
      audio.muted = true;
      audio.src = clipUrl(primeKey);
      var mine = audio.src;
      var p = audio.play();
      // The pause only fires if nothing has taken the player over in the meantime. A
      // steward who taps and scans in the same second would otherwise have this cleanup
      // stop the first guest's greeting a beat after it started — and that guest is the
      // one person in the queue whose greeting anybody would be listening for.
      var done = function () {
        try { if (audio.src === mine) audio.pause(); audio.muted = false; } catch (e) {}
      };
      if (p && p.then) p.then(done, done); else done();
    } catch (e) { try { audio.muted = false; } catch (e2) {} }
  }

  // `once`, and on the capture phase, so it fires before any handler that stops the
  // event — the keypad and the log both do.
  document.addEventListener('pointerdown', unlock, { capture: true, once: true });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', unlock, { capture: true, once: true });

  function greet(key) {
    if (!audio || !key) return;
    try {
      audio.muted = false;
      audio.src = clipUrl(key);
      var p = audio.play();
      if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function () {
        // REFUSED — and this is the one place it is worth saying so. Silently swallowed
        // it is indistinguishable from a muted phone, a missing clip or the voice being
        // switched off, and the steward has no way to tell and nothing to try. One tap
        // fixes it for the whole evening, so offer the tap.
        pending = key;
        el.sound.hidden = false;
      });
    } catch (e) { /* a door with no sound is a working door */ }
  }

  // ══ THE LIGHT ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  function restart(node, css) {
    if (!node) return;
    node.style.animation = 'none';
    void node.offsetWidth;            // reflow, or the reassignment is coalesced away
    node.style.animation = css;
  }

  /** One acknowledgement per scan that settles by itself. */
  function flare() {
    restart(aura, 'dr-flare 1.8s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1) forwards, '
                + 'dr-breathe 9s ease-in-out 1.8s infinite');
  }

  // ══ THE VERDICT ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  // Copy lives here, in one table, because it is the screen's entire vocabulary and a
  // sentence spread across four branches is how two states come to say the same thing.
  // Each carries a distinct WORD and a distinct MARK, so the frame's colour is
  // confirmation rather than information — a steward with any kind of colour vision, or
  // a phone in direct sun, reads the same verdict.
  var SAY = {
    admit:     { mark: '✓', kicker: 'Let them in',     word: 'Admit' },
    honour:    { mark: '★', kicker: 'Guest of honour', word: 'Admit' },
    ask:       { mark: '',  kicker: 'How many',        word: '' },
    duplicate: { mark: '!', kicker: 'Stop and look',   word: 'Already in' },
    refuse:    { mark: '✕', kicker: 'Stop and look',   word: 'No ticket' },
    held:      { mark: '⋯', kicker: 'Not checked',     word: 'Recorded' },
    undone:    { mark: '↩', kicker: 'Taken back',      word: 'Un-admitted' },
    // The rate limiter. The design has no state for it, so it borrows refuse's light —
    // it IS a refusal — and takes its word and detail from the server, which is the only
    // thing that knows how long the steward has to wait.
    slow:      { mark: '»', kicker: 'Slow down',       word: 'Too fast' }
  };

  var LOGWORD  = { admit: 'in', honour: 'in', duplicate: 'again', refuse: 'no',
                   held: 'held', undone: 'back', slow: 'no' };

  var cur = null;          // the verdict on screen, or null
  var onCode = '';         // the code the undo would reverse
  var armed = false;
  var busy = false;
  var dismissAt = null;

  // The verdict is the SERVER's, and `ask` is one of its answers rather than something
  // the browser works out from a seat count. A door that decided locally when to stop and
  // ask could be talked out of stopping — by a stale page, by an offline queue, or by a
  // second gate — and the whole point of the question is that nobody is admitted until it
  // has been answered.
  function kindOf(v) {
    if (!v) return 'idle';
    if (v.verdict === 'admit' && v.honour) return 'honour';
    return v.verdict || 'refuse';
  }

  function setState(k) { root.setAttribute('data-state', k); }

  function clear() {
    cur = null; armed = false;
    if (dismissAt) { clearTimeout(dismissAt); dismissAt = null; }
    slab.hidden = true;
    root.classList.remove('is-frozen');
    el.undo.classList.remove('is-armed');
    setState('idle');
  }

  /**
   * Draw a server verdict.
   *
   * Nothing here decides anything. `kind` is the server's; the client owns the
   * presentation, the arming of undo and the offline queue, and nothing else. A door that
   * inferred "admit" locally would be guessing on the steward's behalf.
   */
  function paint(v) {
    var kind = kindOf(v);
    var say  = SAY[kind] || SAY.refuse;

    cur = v;
    armed = false;
    el.undo.classList.remove('is-armed');
    el.undo.textContent = 'Not them — take it back';

    setState(kind);
    root.classList.add('is-frozen');

    el.mark.textContent = say.mark;
    el.mark.hidden = say.mark === '';
    el.kicker.textContent = say.kicker;
    el.code.textContent = v.code || '';

    // `ask` names the size of the party and `slow` is the server's own sentence; every
    // other word is fixed copy.
    el.word.textContent = kind === 'ask'
      ? 'Party of ' + Number(v.seats || 0)
      : (kind === 'slow' ? (v.title || say.word) : say.word);

    var name = v.name || '';
    el.name.textContent = name;
    el.name.hidden = name === '';
    el.name.classList.toggle('is-honour', kind === 'honour');

    el.meta.textContent = metaFor(kind, v);
    el.meta.hidden = el.meta.textContent === '';

    party(kind, v);
    el.undo.hidden = !(kind === 'admit');

    slab.hidden = false;
    restart(slab, (kind === 'refuse' || kind === 'duplicate' || kind === 'held' || kind === 'slow')
      ? 'dr-nudge .3s ease-in-out'
      : 'dr-rise .3s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1)');
    restart(el.rule, 'dr-rule .55s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1)');
    flare();

    if (kind === 'admit' || kind === 'honour') { onCode = v.code || ''; greet(v.welcome); }
    if (typeof v.admitted === 'number') tally(v.admitted);

    // A queue should not need a tap per guest, so a verdict clears itself — except the
    // two that say STOP AND LOOK, and the one waiting on a count. Those are the states
    // where the steward has something to do, and a screen that wipes itself mid-decision
    // is worse than one tap.
    if (kind === 'admit' || kind === 'honour' || kind === 'undone') {
      dismissAt = setTimeout(clear, 6000);
    }
  }

  function metaFor(kind, v) {
    var seats = Number(v.seats || 0), left = Number(v.seats_left || 0), took = Number(v.admitted_now || 0);

    if (kind === 'honour') return v.detail || 'Received as a guest of honour.';
    if (kind === 'admit') {
      if (seats > 1) return took + ' of ' + seats + ' seats · ' + left + ' still to come';
      return (v.tier ? v.tier : 'Standard') + ' · seat 1 of 1';
    }
    if (kind === 'ask')       return left + ' of ' + seats + ' still to come — how many are here?';
    // The check-in clock comes pre-formatted in the EVENT's zone; a browser formatting the
    // stored value would show a steward in Lagos an hour that never happened.
    if (kind === 'duplicate') return 'Came in ' + (v.at_short || '') + (v.via_label ? ' · ' + v.via_label : '');
    if (kind === 'refuse')    return 'This code is not on tonight’s event.';
    // ── THE ONE PLACE THIS DEPARTS FROM THE DESIGN'S COPY ─────────────────
    //
    // The handoff gives "The gate is offline. Checked the moment the line is back." —
    // which describes a system state, and the same document's copy rule says the sentence
    // must tell the steward what to DO. Offline, the steward IS the check: nothing has
    // verified this ticket and nothing will until the line returns. A line that omits
    // that leaves them to guess whether to let the person in, which is the one decision
    // this screen exists to take off them.
    if (kind === 'held')      return 'The gate is offline. Check the ticket yourself and let '
                                   + 'them through if it looks right — it is checked the moment '
                                   + 'the line is back.';
    if (kind === 'undone')    return 'Their seat is back and the arrivals log says so.';
    return v.detail || '';
  }

  function party(kind, v) {
    el.party.innerHTML = '';
    el.party.hidden = kind !== 'ask';
    if (kind !== 'ask') return;

    var left = Number(v.seats_left || 0), code = v.code || '';
    var add = function (n, label, all) {
      var b = document.createElement('button');
      b.type = 'button';
      b.textContent = label;
      if (all) b.className = 'is-all';
      b.addEventListener('click', function () { check(code, n); });
      el.party.appendChild(b);
    };
    add(left, 'All ' + left, true);
    for (var i = Math.min(left - 1, 3); i >= 1; i--) add(i, String(i), false);
  }

  function tally(n) {
    el.count.textContent = String(n);
    el.countSr.textContent = n + ' of ' + el.count.parentNode.querySelector('i').textContent.slice(1) + ' in';
  }

  // ══ ARRIVALS ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  var log = {{ arrivals|default([])|json_encode|raw }};

  function remember(v, seatsNote) {
    var kind = kindOf(v);
    log.unshift({
      t: clock(),
      v: LOGWORD[kind] || 'no',
      n: (v.name || v.code || '') + (seatsNote || '')
    });
    log = log.slice(0, 200);
    drawLog();
  }

  function clock() {
    var d = new Date(), p = function (n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; };
    return p(d.getHours()) + ':' + p(d.getMinutes());
  }

  function drawLog() {
    el.last.textContent = log.length ? (log[0].t + ' · ' + log[0].n) : 'Nothing scanned yet tonight';
    el.logN.textContent = log.length + (log.length === 1 ? ' entry' : ' entries');
    el.logE.hidden = log.length !== 0;

    var frag = document.createDocumentFragment();
    for (var i = 0; i < log.length; i++) {
      var r = log[i];
      var row = document.createElement('div'); row.className = 'dr__row';
      var t = document.createElement('span'); t.className = 'dr__row__t'; t.textContent = r.t;
      var n = document.createElement('span'); n.className = 'dr__row__n'; n.textContent = r.n;
      var w = document.createElement('span'); w.className = 'dr__row__v';
      w.setAttribute('data-v', r.v); w.textContent = r.v;
      row.appendChild(t); row.appendChild(n); row.appendChild(w);
      frag.appendChild(row);
    }
    el.rows.innerHTML = '';
    el.rows.appendChild(frag);
  }

  // ══ THE OFFLINE QUEUE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
  //
  // Keyed to this pass, so two gates on one borrowed phone never flush each other's
  // scans. The door must never show `Admit` on a guess: a queued scan is RECORDED and
  // said to be unchecked, which is a different promise and the only honest one.
  var QKEY = 'ag-door-q:' + TOKEN.slice(0, 12);
  var pending = [];

  function qLoad() {
    try { var raw = localStorage.getItem(QKEY); pending = raw ? (JSON.parse(raw) || []) : []; }
    catch (e) { pending = []; }
    if (!Array.isArray(pending)) pending = [];
    paintPending();
  }
  function qSave() {
    try { localStorage.setItem(QKEY, JSON.stringify(pending)); }
    catch (e) { /* a full or disabled store must not stop the door; the queue lives in memory */ }
    paintPending();
  }
  function paintPending() {
    el.held.hidden = pending.length === 0;
    el.heldT.textContent = pending.length
      + (pending.length === 1 ? ' scan held — not checked yet' : ' scans held — not checked yet');
  }
  function qAdd(code, seats) {
    pending.push({
      // A client id, so a flush that half-succeeds or is retried after a timeout cannot
      // record the same person twice.
      id: (Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)),
      code: code,
      seats: Number(seats || 0),
      // The moment it HAPPENED. Sent so the log reads as an evening rather than as forty
      // people arriving in the same second half an hour later.
      at: stamp()
    });
    qSave();
  }
  function stamp() {
    var d = new Date(), p = function (n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; };
    return d.getFullYear() + '-' + p(d.getMonth() + 1) + '-' + p(d.getDate()) + ' '
         + p(d.getHours()) + ':' + p(d.getMinutes()) + ':' + p(d.getSeconds());
  }

  var flushing = false;
  async function flush() {
    if (flushing || !pending.length) return;
    flushing = true;
    var sending = pending.slice(0, 200);
    try {
      var r = await fetch(URL_SYNC, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ scans: sending })
      });
      var d = await r.json();
      var done = {};
      (d.results || []).forEach(function (x) { if (x && x.id) done[x.id] = x; });
      pending = pending.filter(function (i) { return !done[i.id]; });
      qSave();
      if (typeof d.admitted === 'number') tally(d.admitted);
      (d.results || []).forEach(function (x) {
        if (x && x.verdict) remember({ verdict: x.verdict, name: x.name || '', code: x.code || '' });
      });
    } catch (e) { /* still down; the queue keeps it and the strip keeps saying so */ }
    flushing = false;
  }

  // ══ CHECKING ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  async function check(code, seats) {
    code = (code || '').trim();
    if (!code || busy) return;
    busy = true; el.go.disabled = true;

    try {
      var r = await fetch(URL_CHECK, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ code: code, seats: Number(seats || 0) })
      });
      var v = await r.json();
      paint(v);
      // `ask` is a QUESTION, not an arrival. Writing it to the log put a name in the list
      // and on the dock's last line for somebody standing in front of the steward who had
      // not been admitted, refused, or anything else — and it was logged as a refusal,
      // because `ask` has no word in the log's vocabulary and the fallback is 'no'.
      if (kindOf(v) !== 'ask') {
        remember(v, (Number(v.seats || 0) > 1 && v.verdict === 'admit')
          ? ' · ' + Number(v.admitted_now || 0) + ' of ' + Number(v.seats || 0) : '');
      }
    } catch (e) {
      // The line is down. RECORD it and keep the queue moving — and say exactly what that
      // means, because this is the one verdict the door does not know the answer to.
      qAdd(code, Number(seats || 0));
      paint({ verdict: 'held', code: code });
      remember({ verdict: 'held', code: code });
    }

    el.input.value = '';
    busy = false; el.go.disabled = false;
  }

  el.form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    // READ BEFORE CLOSING. `closePad()` empties the field, so passing `el.input.value`
    // after it hands `check()` an empty string and it returns without asking anything —
    // the keypad looked completely normal and did nothing at all, on the one path every
    // iOS phone depends on.
    var code = el.input.value;
    closePad();
    check(code);
  });

  el.dismiss.addEventListener('click', clear);

  el.undo.addEventListener('click', async function () {
    if (!onCode || busy) return;

    if (!armed) {
      armed = true;
      el.undo.classList.add('is-armed');
      // First name only: the full name overruns the pill at 400px, and the point is that
      // it names a person rather than which person exactly.
      var first = (cur && cur.name) ? String(cur.name).split(/\s+/)[0] : 'them';
      el.undo.textContent = 'Press again to un-admit ' + first;
      if (dismissAt) { clearTimeout(dismissAt); dismissAt = null; }
      return;
    }

    busy = true; el.undo.disabled = true;
    try {
      var r = await fetch(URL_UNDO, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Requested-With': 'XMLHttpRequest' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ code: onCode })
      });
      var v = await r.json();
      paint(v); remember(v);
    } catch (e) {
      paint({ verdict: 'refuse', code: onCode, detail: 'Nothing was changed. Scan again and retry.' });
    }
    busy = false; el.undo.disabled = false;
  });

  // ══ SHEETS — mutually exclusive, and the keypad clears the verdict ══════

  function openPad() {
    closeLog();
    clear();
    el.pad.hidden = false;
    root.classList.add('is-frozen');
    el.input.focus();
  }
  function closePad() {
    el.pad.hidden = true;
    el.input.value = '';
    if (!cur) root.classList.remove('is-frozen');
  }
  function openLog()  { closePad(); el.log.hidden = false; el.closeLog.focus(); }
  function closeLog() { el.log.hidden = true; }

  // The tap that fixes the evening. Playing the greeting HERE — inside the gesture — both
  // greets the guest standing there and leaves the element unlocked for every guest after.
  el.sound.addEventListener('click', function () {
    unlocked = true;
    el.sound.hidden = true;
    var key = pending; pending = '';
    if (key) greet(key);
  });

  el.openPad.addEventListener('click', openPad);
  el.closePad.addEventListener('click', closePad);
  el.openLog.addEventListener('click', openLog);
  el.closeLog.addEventListener('click', closeLog);
  el.send.addEventListener('click', function () { flush(); });

  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key !== 'Escape') return;
    if (!el.log.hidden) closeLog();
    else if (!el.pad.hidden) closePad();
    else if (cur) clear();
  });

  // ══ COMING BACK ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  //
  // Three ways, because none is reliable alone at a venue: `online` does not fire on
  // every recovery, and `navigator.onLine` reports the wifi association rather than
  // whether anything is reachable through it — a captive portal is "online" and useless.
  // So the browser's hint, a slow poll, and a button the steward can press.
  qLoad();
  drawLog();
  flush();
  window.addEventListener('online', function () { flush(); });
  setInterval(function () { if (pending.length) flush(); }, 20000);

  // ══ THE CAMERA ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  //
  // TWO THINGS KEPT THIS FROM EVER WORKING IN PRODUCTION, and both failed silently.
  //
  //   1. `Permissions-Policy: camera=()` denied the camera on every page of the site.
  //      getUserMedia was rejected before any of this ran, and the catch wrote "Camera
  //      unavailable" — indistinguishable from a refused prompt or a broken lens.
  //   2. The camera was gated on `BarcodeDetector`, which exists on no iOS browser (they
  //      are all WebKit) and not on Firefox. A steward holding an iPhone saw no camera at
  //      all, which at a Nigerian gala is a large share of the people working a gate.
  //
  // So the gate is getUserMedia alone, and WHICH decoder runs is decided after the stream
  // opens: the native one where it exists, jsQR where it does not. jsQR is vendored and
  // lazy — a door on venue wifi cannot fetch a third-party script the moment a queue
  // forms, and a Chrome phone should not download 130KB it never uses.
  var vid = el.video;
  var secure = window.isSecureContext || location.hostname === 'localhost';
  var stream = null, timer = null, native = null, jsqr = null, canvas = null, ctx = null;
  var lastRaw = '', lastAt = 0;

  function offer(msg) {
    el.tapT.textContent = msg;
    el.tap.hidden = false;
  }

  async function nativeDecoder() {
    if (!('BarcodeDetector' in window)) return null;
    try {
      var f = await BarcodeDetector.getSupportedFormats();
      if (f.indexOf('qr_code') === -1) return null;
      return new BarcodeDetector({ formats: ['qr_code'] });
    } catch (e) { return null; }
  }

  function loadJsQR() {
    if (window.jsQR) return Promise.resolve(window.jsQR);
    return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {
      var s = document.createElement('script');
      // The nonce is carried deliberately. `script-src` is `'self'` plus a nonce, so a
      // same-origin src loads without it today — but the day this policy gains
      // `strict-dynamic`, host sources stop applying and an un-nonced injected script is
      // refused. The failure then is a scanner that stops working on exactly the phones
      // that need it, months after the change that did it.
      s.nonce = NONCE;
      s.src = '/assets/vendor/jsqr.min.js';
      s.onload = function () { resolve(window.jsQR || null); };
      s.onerror = function () { reject(new Error('decoder')); };
      document.head.appendChild(s);
    });
  }

  async function readFrame() {
    if (native) {
      var found = await native.detect(vid);
      return (found && found.length) ? String(found[0].rawValue || '') : '';
    }
    if (!jsqr) return '';
    var w = vid.videoWidth, h = vid.videoHeight;
    if (!w || !h) return '';
    if (!canvas) { canvas = document.createElement('canvas'); ctx = canvas.getContext('2d', { willReadFrequently: true }); }
    if (canvas.width !== w) { canvas.width = w; canvas.height = h; }
    ctx.drawImage(vid, 0, 0, w, h);
    // A QR symbol decodes from its geometry, so the frame is sized to the VIDEO's own
    // dimensions and not the element's — a CSS-scaled video hands the decoder a stretched
    // image it cannot read.
    var r = jsqr(ctx.getImageData(0, 0, w, h).data, w, h, { inversionAttempts: 'dontInvert' });
    return r && r.data ? String(r.data) : '';
  }

  async function startCamera() {
    if (stream) return true;
    if (!secure || !navigator.mediaDevices || !navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia) {
      offer('No camera here — type the code');
      return false;
    }
    try {
      // The REAR camera: the steward holds the phone and the ticket faces it.
      stream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({
        video: { facingMode: { ideal: 'environment' } }, audio: false });
      vid.srcObject = stream;
      vid.setAttribute('playsinline', '');   // iOS will not start an inline video without it
      await vid.play();
    } catch (e) {
      stream = null;
      // NAMED, because "unavailable" sent an operator to the wrong fix for two of these.
      var n = (e && e.name) || '';
      offer(n === 'NotAllowedError'  ? 'Camera blocked — allow it, then tap'
          : n === 'NotFoundError'    ? 'No camera on this phone — type the code'
          : n === 'NotReadableError' ? 'Another app has the camera — close it and tap'
          : 'Tap to start the camera');
      return false;
    }

    native = await nativeDecoder();
    if (!native) {
      try { jsqr = await loadJsQR(); } catch (e) { jsqr = null; }
      if (!jsqr) { stopCamera(); offer('The scanner would not load — type the code'); return false; }
    }

    el.tap.hidden = true;
    timer = setInterval(async function () {
      if (busy || cur || !el.pad.hidden || vid.readyState < 2) return;
      try {
        var raw = (await readFrame()).trim();
        if (!raw) return;
        // A camera pointed at one ticket fires many times a second. The same code inside
        // three seconds is the same person, and re-sending it would report them as a
        // duplicate of themselves — the one wrong answer that looks like fraud.
        var now = Date.now();
        if (raw === lastRaw && now - lastAt < 3000) return;
        lastRaw = raw; lastAt = now;
        check(raw);
      } catch (e) { /* a bad frame is not an error */ }
    }, native ? 300 : 180);
    return true;
  }

  function stopCamera() {
    if (stream) { stream.getTracks().forEach(function (t) { t.stop(); }); stream = null; }
    if (timer) { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; }
  }

  el.tap.addEventListener('click', function () { el.tap.hidden = true; startCamera(); });

  // ── THE TORCH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Only where the track advertises it. A button that does nothing on a phone whose
  // camera has no lamp is worse than no button, so it hides itself rather than lying.
  var torchOn = false;
  el.torch.addEventListener('click', async function () {
    if (!stream) return;
    var track = stream.getVideoTracks()[0];
    if (!track || typeof track.applyConstraints !== 'function') return;
    try {
      torchOn = !torchOn;
      await track.applyConstraints({ advanced: [{ torch: torchOn }] });
      el.torch.classList.toggle('is-on', torchOn);
      el.torch.setAttribute('aria-pressed', torchOn ? 'true' : 'false');
    } catch (e) { torchOn = false; el.torch.classList.remove('is-on'); }
  });

  // A camera left running behind a locked screen is a flat battery an hour into a gala.
  document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
    if (document.hidden) stopCamera();
    else if (!stream && el.tap.hidden) startCamera();
  });

  startCamera();

})();
</script>
{% endif %}

</body>
</html>
